## 2. Encrypted `.env` Sync

### Problem

`.env` is gitignored. When secrets change on one machine, the other machine has stale env vars until manually updated. This caused `MATTERMOST_PASSTHROUGH_SECRET` and other keys to be missing on the laptop.

### Solution

AES-256-CBC encrypted `.env.enc` file committed to git. Both machines share a passphrase via `.env.key` (gitignored, set up once per machine).

### How it works

| Step | Action | File |
|------|--------|------|
| `go.ps1` after `git pull` | Auto-decrypts `.env.enc` -> `.env` (skips if `.env` is newer) | `Go-EnvSync.ps1` |
| Morning sync before `git add` | Auto-encrypts `.env` -> `.env.enc` so encrypted copy is staged | `Go-MorningSync.ps1` |

### File format

`.env.enc` = 16-byte IV + AES-256-CBC ciphertext. Key = SHA-256 of passphrase from `.env.key`.

### Setup (one-time per machine)

```powershell
Set-Content 'F:\PolySaaS\.env.key' 'PolySaaS-Sync-2026'
```

Use the **same passphrase** on every machine. The `.env.key` file is gitignored.

### Files created/changed

- `scripts/go/Go-EnvSync.ps1` — `Protect-PolySaaSEnv` (encrypt) and `Unprotect-PolySaaSEnv` (decrypt)
- `go.ps1` — dot-sources `Go-EnvSync.ps1`, runs decrypt after pull
- `scripts/go/Go-MorningSync.ps1` — runs encrypt before staging
- `.gitignore` — added `.env.key`
- `.env.enc` — first encrypted copy (committed)

### Verified

Round-trip test passed: encrypt -> delete `.env` -> decrypt from `.env.enc` -> byte-for-byte match with original.

